#!/usr/bin/env hirari
"""Run and observe background programs without giving up the shell.
job start "program.exe" (data list "argument" ...) [OPTIONS]
job status ID | job wait ID [TIMEOUT_MS] | job cancel ID | job forget ID | job list
OPTIONS is a record, e.g. (data record -timeout_ms 60000 -directory "C:/work").
A job runs until it exits or is cancelled; only timeout_ms terminates it.
wait never stops a job: its result has wait "completed" or "timeout".
State fields: id state pid stdout stderr exit_status error timed_out elapsed_ms.
Use structured worker messages for progress/results; native output works too.
Jobs belong to this Hirari session and stop when it exits.
"""
apply -(provide -jobs) args?
